@page "/dashboard"
<PageTitle>Dashboard setup — Flywheel</PageTitle>
<article class="docs">
<nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Guides"><Anchor Href="/getting-started/">Runner setup</Anchor><Anchor Href="/dashboard/" aria-current="page">Dashboard setup</Anchor></nav>
<H1>Your jobs, in view.</H1>
<Paragraph>The dashboard is an optional Blazor WebAssembly client. Your browser renders the interface; Flywheel handles API requests and SignalR updates. You can run jobs without the dashboard.</Paragraph>
<H2>Try the demo</H2>
<Paragraph>This demo uses Redis, one of several supported storage mechanisms. To run it, use .NET 10 with Redis at <code>localhost:6379</code>:</Paragraph>
<CodeExample Text="@DemoExample" Label="Run the dashboard demo commands" Language="shell" />
<Paragraph>Open <Anchor Href="https://localhost:7443/">https://localhost:7443</Anchor> and sign in with <code>admin</code> / <code>flywheel-demo</code>. These credentials are for the local Development demo. Press Ctrl+C to stop it.</Paragraph>
<H2>Find and inspect work</H2>
<ol><li>Use the overview to search jobs and filter by state.</li><li>Open a job to inspect its attempts, timing, and captured <code>ILogger</code> output.</li><li>Open Scheduled for pending jobs and retries, or Recurring to inspect schedules and run one now.</li></ol>
<H2>Add it to your application</H2>
<Paragraph>Install the package in a Blazor WebAssembly app:</Paragraph>
<CodeExample Text="@InstallExample" Label="Install the dashboard package command" Language="shell" />
<Paragraph>Register the client in its <code>Program.cs</code>:</Paragraph>
<CodeExample Text="@ClientExample" Label="Dashboard client registration example" Language="csharp" />
<Paragraph>Use the <Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.flywheel.suite/tree/main/test/Soenneker.Flywheel.Dashboard.Demo">WebAssembly demo</Anchor> for the host page, Quark styles, and router. Use <code>FlywheelRouter</code> in the host to match dashboard routes explicitly, without assembly scanning.</Paragraph>
<H2>Connect the server</H2>
<Paragraph>On the ASP.NET Core host, add dashboard services to your Flywheel registration:</Paragraph>
<CodeExample Text="@ServerExample" Label="Dashboard server registration example" Language="csharp" />
<Paragraph>Import <code>Soenneker.Flywheel.Core.Registrars</code>. Configure a PBKDF2 password PHC string, then map the authenticated API and SignalR hub. The <Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.flywheel.suite/blob/main/test/Soenneker.Flywheel.Demo/Program.cs">complete sample server</Anchor> includes password hashing, authentication, rate limiting, and endpoint setup.</Paragraph>
<Paragraph>Serve the client and API over the same HTTPS origin. Static WebAssembly files can be delivered by a CDN or Cloudflare Worker, with API and WebSocket traffic routed to the ASP.NET Core backend. Static hosting alone does not run Flywheel or connect to job storage.</Paragraph>
<Paragraph>UI rendering stays in the browser. API queries and live updates still consume backend resources.</Paragraph>
<H2>Built-in routes</H2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Page</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><code>/flywheel</code></td><td>Activity and job search</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>/signin</code></td><td>Sign in</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>/flywheel/recurring</code></td><td>Recurring schedules</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>/flywheel/scheduled</code></td><td>Pending jobs and retries</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>/jobs/&#123;JobId&#125;</code></td><td>Execution details and logs</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<Paragraph>The default home is <code>/flywheel</code>. With <code>FlywheelRouter</code>, setting <code>HomePath = "/"</code> serves the dashboard at the root without an <code>Index.razor</code> wrapper. Other host pages can be rendered explicitly through its <code>NotFound</code> fragment. See the <Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.flywheel.suite/blob/main/docs/dashboard.md#pages-and-navigation">routing guide</Anchor> to host it at <code>/</code>.</Paragraph>
</article>

@code {
    private const string DemoExample = """
git clone https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.flywheel.suite.git
cd soenneker.flywheel.suite
dotnet dev-certs https --trust
dotnet run --project test/Soenneker.Flywheel.Demo
""";

    private const string InstallExample = """
dotnet add package Soenneker.Flywheel.Dashboard
""";

    private const string ClientExample = """
using Soenneker.Flywheel.Dashboard.Registrars;

builder.Services.AddScoped(_ => new HttpClient
{
    BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress)
});
builder.Services.AddFlywheelDashboardAsScoped();
""";

    private const string ServerExample = """
.AddDashboard(options =>
{
    options.Username = builder.Configuration["Flywheel:Dashboard:Username"]!;
    options.PasswordPhc = builder.Configuration["Flywheel:Dashboard:PasswordPhc"]!;
})
""";
}
